Fillets: a walk whose contact crosses a tangent edge onto a face of the
spine's end that the ball cannot touch rolls on over its face's surface,
is cut by that face and ends in a point on the spine's last edge
(mitcad#1413).

The case: a hub's foot on a flange rounded with 1 between holes whose
walls touch the hub (two reported designs' item replayed). Each hole's rim
was rounded with 0.5 before: a torus around the hole and, between the
torus and the hub, a face along the hub's foot (its edge with the hub the
spine's last edge, up to the vertex where the hole touches the hub), tangent
to the torus across an edge and bending towards the ball more sharply than
the ball. The walk along the foot reached the torus with its contact on the
flange, then that face, where the walk reframed onto it and failed: no ball
of 1 rolls on it. The stored body rolls the ball on over the torus's own
surface past that edge, between it and the hub, cuts the blend by that face
from the crossing, and ends it in a point on the spine's last edge where
the cut meets the contact on the hub; the edge stays sharp from there to
the vertex.

- ChFi3d_TightTangentFaceAtEnd: a contact that left its face F (along no
  edge of the spine) across a tangent edge onto a face B along the spine
  holding the spine's end vertex the walk heads for, where ballCannotTouch
  says no ball of the radius touches B.
- StartSol does not reframe onto such a face, and PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine
  ends the walk in that direction there (or turns back from a start inside).
- WalkedCutToEnd takes such a B as it takes a face at an angle: it walks on
  with F's surface unbounded up to where the other contact reaches its edge
  with B, and cuts the piece by B. The cut starts where the surfaces meet
  tangentially, where GeomInt_IntSS's line stops 0.006 mm short of the
  crossing; ChFi3d_CutBySections finds it section by section of the walked
  surface (the first crossing of B's surface from the other contact's
  side), with its p-curve on B through the feet of its points
  (ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece's BySections).
- PerformFilletOnVertex makes no corner at a vertex where every stripe
  ends in a point of its own short of it (the stripes on both sides of the
  vertex where a hole touches the hub).

